Section: Tweaks
Homepage: https://github.com/ibrahim2100/Albrhi-Repo
Description: No ads, background playback, and a settings panel in Arabic or English.
 .
 ◍ DOWNLOADS
 Not yet. That one is being measured before it is built — see the diagnostics page.
 .
 ▍ NO ADS
 Ads are stopped at three separate points, because they arrive by three separate
 routes and blocking one does nothing about the others.
 .
 First, the app stops telling YouTube it wants ads at all, so they are never sent
 rather than sent and then hidden. Second, promoted rows are dropped out of the feed
 by the identifier YouTube's own servers attach to them — including the plain-looking
 layouts that carry sponsored content without the word "ad" anywhere in them. Third,
 the player refuses ads before a video, in the middle of one, and the kind stitched
 into the stream itself, which nothing else can reach.
 .
 ▍ BACKGROUND PLAYBACK
 Audio keeps going when you leave the app or lock the screen.
 .
 ▍ QUIETER
 Silence the prompt to update — updating replaces the app and removes this tweak. And
 optionally hide the paid-promotion banner, off by default, because it is a disclosure.
 .
 ▍ SETTINGS
 Hold two fingers anywhere in YouTube. Full Arabic and English with right-to-left
 layout, and a card at the top that says whether everything actually attached to your
 build rather than leaving you to wonder.
 .
 ▍ DIAGNOSTICS
 Reports what the tweak finds in your copy of YouTube and what YouTube said about the
 last video you played. Also written to Documents/AlbrhiYT-report.txt, so it is
 readable even if nothing else worked.
 .
 ▍ TESTED ON
 YouTube 21.30.5. Nothing is pinned to a version number: every class is looked up at
 runtime and skipped if it is not there. The hooks are on YouTube's model and service
 layer rather than its views — views get renamed and rewritten between releases, and a
 tweak that hooks them quietly stops working. A player response does not.
 .
 Developed by Ibrahim Ismail AL-Rahn. Free and open source under the GNU GPL v3.
